<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       PYRELANDS_MECHANICS_1, mechanism 3 — how the fire-hawk gets to decide.

       Uses vanilla's own supported modder insertion hook: Core's
       Defs/ThinkTreeDefs/Animal.xml carries
       <li Class="ThinkNode_SubtreesByTag"><insertTag>Animal_PreWander</insertTag></li>,
       and a ThinkTreeDef declaring that insertTag is spliced in there. Not a
       Harmony transpiler and not a PatchOperation into the vanilla Animal tree.
       Same mechanism, same tag, as this repo's own animal-behaviour precedent:
       src/RimMandrake/RimProperty/Defs/AnimalTheft/ThinkTreeDefs_AnimalSteal.xml
       (which documents the hook at length). No MayRequire: Animal_PreWander is
       Core.

       NO FACTION GATE, deliberately. §7d rules the hawk tameable and rules what
       that costs: "the fire a tamed hawk spreads is still nobody's friend."
       A tamed hawk therefore carries twigs in your base exactly as a wild one
       does. Adding a ThinkNode_ConditionalHasFaction wrapper here would quietly
       undo that ruling.

       The species gate is the comp (CompFireHawkSpread), checked in C# by the
       job-giver — there is no per-species XML hook at this splice point, the
       same reason JobGiver_RM_WildSteal gives for checking its own marker in
       code. That is also what makes a second twig-carrier cost one XML node
       and no C#.

       insertPriority 55: above RimProperty's theft nodes (50) so a hawk that is
       both a thief and an igniter reaches for the fire first. Nothing else in
       this repo inserts at this tag.
  ======================================================================== -->
  <ThinkTreeDef>
    <defName>RUT_FireHawk_CarryEmber</defName>
    <insertTag>Animal_PreWander</insertTag>
    <insertPriority>55</insertPriority>
    <thinkRoot Class="ThinkNode_Tagger">
      <tagToGive>Misc</tagToGive>
      <subNodes>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.PyrelandsMechanics.JobGiver_RUT_FireHawkCarryEmber" />
      </subNodes>
    </thinkRoot>
  </ThinkTreeDef>

</Defs>
